From 06b614c0355ee6fd1d38246989d64a711f126292 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: scada <scada@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:04:55 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 54/78] ASoC: qdsp6: q6core: don't query versions on the
 MSM8998 ADSP

AVCS_CMD_GET_FWK_VERSION wedges the MSM8998 ADSP firmware: it stops
consuming its glink FIFO at that message, with no crash and no watchdog
bite, after which no APR, QMI or SLIMbus traffic gets through and no
sound card appears. Skip the version query on MSM8998 so AFE, ASM and
ADM fall back to their legacy APIs.

With the query skipped the SLIMbus NGD comes up, the WCD934x enumerates
and the LG-V30 card plays on the loudspeaker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0144VMKxYe33NKa3LLPZNivr
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
index 49cfb32cd209..fa81b19bd324 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6core.c
@@ -253,6 +253,17 @@ int q6core_get_svc_api_info(int svc_id, struct q6core_svc_api_info *ainfo)
 		return 0;
 
 	mutex_lock(&g_core->lock);
+	/*
+	 * The MSM8998 ADSP firmware stops reading its glink FIFO for good
+	 * when it receives AVCS_CMD_GET_FWK_VERSION: no crash, no watchdog,
+	 * just a dead transport that also takes the SLIMbus QMI service with
+	 * it. Leave the versions unknown there; AFE, ASM and ADM then use
+	 * their legacy APIs, which this firmware speaks.
+	 */
+	if (!g_core->is_version_requested &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,msm8998"))
+		g_core->is_version_requested = true;
+
 	if (!g_core->is_version_requested) {
 		if (q6core_get_fwk_versions(g_core) == -ENOTSUPP)
 			q6core_get_svc_versions(g_core);
